    "material_one": "(5120,12288) at rows 128 straddles parity: 0.970 in the 15-rep all-shapes sweep and 1.022 in the 20-rep pin-down. The promotion band for that shape is therefore strongly supported only through rows 112; at rows 128 the effect is inside measurement noise and could be a small regression.",
    "material_two": "(5120,12288) at rows 67 measured 1.106 and 1.075, and (5120,10240) at rows 128 measured 1.083 and 1.110. Both runs win in every measurement, so only the quoted digit changes.",
    "correction_reason": "the first version of this artifact merged points from the 15-rep all-shapes sweep and the 20-rep pin-down runs into a single per-shape table without labelling which run each point came from, and cited the pin-down value for (5120,12288) rows 67/128 in a table that read like the sweep. Every individual number was a real measurement, but the table was not one consistent protocol, and the unlabelled merge happened to flatter the (5120,12288) band edge.",
    "code_left_unchanged": "GGUF_Q4_T16_PHYSICAL_SINGLE_WAVE_MAX_ROWS stays at 128 for all three shapes. Narrowing (5120,12288) to 112 on the strength of one of two disagreeing runs would be fitting the band to a single measurement; resolving it needs repeats at rows 120-128 for that shape, which is recorded as the next step."
  }
